### PayFlow demo walkthrough
### Run each request in order with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Start everything first:  docker compose --profile apps up -d --build

@payments = http://127.0.0.1:8080/api
@ledger = http://127.0.0.1:8081/api/ledger
@fraud = http://127.0.0.1:8082/api

### 1. maker1 creates a small payment -> APPROVED straight away (fraud check said ALLOW)
# @name small
POST {{payments}}/payments
Authorization: Basic maker1 maker1-pass
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-small-1

{"debtorAccount": "ACC10001", "creditorAccount": "ACC20002", "amount": 150.00, "currency": "USD"}

### 2. Same request again -> 200 + Idempotent-Replayed: true, same payment ID, no second charge
POST {{payments}}/payments
Authorization: Basic maker1 maker1-pass
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-small-1

{"debtorAccount": "ACC10001", "creditorAccount": "ACC20002", "amount": 150.00, "currency": "USD"}

### 3. A second later the ledger has booked it and the payment is SETTLED
GET {{payments}}/payments/{{small.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Basic auditor1 auditor1-pass

### 4. The double entry in the ledger: one DEBIT, one CREDIT, same amount
GET {{ledger}}/postings/{{small.response.body.id}}

### 5. Balances: ACC10001 is -150.00, ACC20002 is +150.00
GET {{ledger}}/accounts/ACC10001/balances

### 6. Trial balance: total debits == total credits
GET {{ledger}}/trial-balance

### 7. A large payment is held for a checker
# @name large
POST {{payments}}/payments
Authorization: Basic lead1 lead1-pass
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-large-1

{"debtorAccount": "ACC10001", "creditorAccount": "ACC30003", "amount": 25000.00, "currency": "USD"}

### 8. lead1 has the CHECKER role too, but can't approve their own payment -> 403
POST {{payments}}/payments/{{large.response.body.id}}/approve
Authorization: Basic lead1 lead1-pass

### 9. A different checker can -> APPROVED, then SETTLED once the ledger books it
POST {{payments}}/payments/{{large.response.body.id}}/approve
Authorization: Basic checker1 checker1-pass

### 10. Make the fraud service fail every call (chaos mode)
PUT {{fraud}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{"failureRate": 1.0, "delayMs": 0}

### 11. Payments are now held for manual review instead of failing or being approved blindly.
###     Send this 3 times with new keys: after ~5 failed calls the circuit breaker opens and
###     payment-service stops calling the fraud service for 30s (watch its log).
POST {{payments}}/payments
Authorization: Basic maker1 maker1-pass
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-chaos-{{$guid}}

{"debtorAccount": "ACC10001", "creditorAccount": "ACC40004", "amount": 20.00, "currency": "USD"}

### 12. Turn chaos mode off again
PUT {{fraud}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{"failureRate": 0, "delayMs": 0}

### 13. Run reconciliation for the last 24 hours -> MATCHED
POST {{payments}}/reconciliation/runs
Authorization: Basic auditor1 auditor1-pass

### 14. Metrics in Prometheus format
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/actuator/prometheus
